ROUND-4 B1.4 — CLOSED. The retry no longer lands.
--------------------------------------------------
This was the one thing that had to hold, and it holds. Same lab shape as
round 4's lab3, real CLI, nothing done between invocations:

  lab3 (local only, strategy rebase, studio inside the repo, certificate
  tree:deadbeef... on gate "tests"):
    merge #1 -> "opus/W-900 was rebased onto master — ... certifies
                 tree:deadbeef..., which no longer matches the rebased tree
                 (tree:84b819e3...); check out opus/W-900 and re-run
                 'bisellium verify W-900' there, then retry the merge"  exit 1
    merge #2 -> "opus/W-900's tree no longer matches its certificate — ..."
                                                                       exit 1
    merge #3 -> same                                                   exit 1
    master: 2 commits (init, trunk moved). opus/W-900 still present.
    Certificate untouched.
  The second and third runs take the non-rebased wording, which is the
  `rebased` parameter doing its only job. Correct.

  lab4 (the studio's own configured flow: rebase + push + pull_after_push +
  pr.required, live bare origin, the opus branch pushed BEFORE the trunk
  moved — the PR-already-open case):
    merge #1/#2/#3 all exit 1. Across all three runs
      origin opus/W-900 stayed 6c7ab31 (its pre-rebase tip),
      origin master stayed 2fa2081,
      local master stayed at "trunk moved".
    The refusal precedes the push on every run, not just the first.

Mutation confirms the relocation is what does it, not luck:
  M-G  restore the round-4 placement (`if (staleError && rebased) return`)
       -> 4 FAIL, and exactly the right four: behaviour 23's
